{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A query function can be any function that returns a promise. The promise should resolve data or throw an error."}]},{"type":"code","value":"createQueryController(this, {\n  queryKey: ['todos'],\n  queryFn: fetchTodos,\n})\n\ncreateQueryController(this, () => ({\n  queryKey: ['todo', this.todoId],\n  queryFn: () => fetchTodo(this.todoId),\n}))","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"handling-errors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Handling Errors"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Query needs failed query functions to throw or return a rejected promise. Some clients do that automatically. The browser "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetch"},{"type":"text","value":" API does not, so check "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"response.ok"},{"type":"text","value":" yourself:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"async function fetchTodos(): Promise<Todo[]> {\n  const response = await fetch('/api/todos')\n\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    throw new Error('Failed to fetch todos')\n  }\n\n  return response.json() as Promise<Todo[]>\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The thrown error is available on the query result:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const query = this.todos()\n\nif (query.isError) {\n  return html`Error: ${query.error.message}`\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"query-function-context","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query Function Context"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Query passes a context object to every query function. It includes:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":": the current query key"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"client"},{"type":"text","value":": the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"signal"},{"type":"text","value":": an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AbortSignal"},{"type":"text","value":" for cancellation"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"meta"},{"type":"text","value":": optional query metadata"}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"createQueryController(this, {\n  queryKey: ['todos', { status: 'open' }],\n  queryFn: async ({ queryKey, signal }) => {\n    const [, filters] = queryKey\n    const response = await fetch(`/api/todos?status=${filters.status}`, {\n      signal,\n    })\n    if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Failed to fetch todos')\n    return response.json() as Promise<Todo[]>\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Infinite query functions also receive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pageParam"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"createInfiniteQueryController(this, {\n  queryKey: ['projects'],\n  queryFn: ({ pageParam }) => fetchProjectsPage(pageParam),\n  initialPageParam: 1,\n  getNextPageParam: (lastPage) =>\n    lastPage.hasMore ? lastPage.page + 1 : undefined,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"./infinite-queries.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Infinite Queries"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the controller-specific behavior."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"handling-errors","text":"Handling Errors","level":2},{"id":"query-function-context","text":"Query Function Context","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nA query function can be any function that returns a promise. The promise should resolve data or throw an error.\n\n```ts\ncreateQueryController(this, {\n  queryKey: ['todos'],\n  queryFn: fetchTodos,\n})\n\ncreateQueryController(this, () => ({\n  queryKey: ['todo', this.todoId],\n  queryFn: () => fetchTodo(this.todoId),\n}))\n```\n\n## Handling Errors\n\nTanStack Query needs failed query functions to throw or return a rejected promise. Some clients do that automatically. The browser `fetch` API does not, so check `response.ok` yourself:\n\n```ts\nasync function fetchTodos(): Promise<Todo[]> {\n  const response = await fetch('/api/todos')\n\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    throw new Error('Failed to fetch todos')\n  }\n\n  return response.json() as Promise<Todo[]>\n}\n```\n\nThe thrown error is available on the query result:\n\n```ts\nconst query = this.todos()\n\nif (query.isError) {\n  return html`Error: ${query.error.message}`\n}\n```\n\n## Query Function Context\n\nTanStack Query passes a context object to every query function. It includes:\n\n- `queryKey`: the current query key\n- `client`: the `QueryClient`\n- `signal`: an `AbortSignal` for cancellation\n- `meta`: optional query metadata\n\n```ts\ncreateQueryController(this, {\n  queryKey: ['todos', { status: 'open' }],\n  queryFn: async ({ queryKey, signal }) => {\n    const [, filters] = queryKey\n    const response = await fetch(`/api/todos?status=${filters.status}`, {\n      signal,\n    })\n    if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Failed to fetch todos')\n    return response.json() as Promise<Todo[]>\n  },\n})\n```\n\nInfinite query functions also receive `pageParam`:\n\n```ts\ncreateInfiniteQueryController(this, {\n  queryKey: ['projects'],\n  queryFn: ({ pageParam }) => fetchProjectsPage(pageParam),\n  initialPageParam: 1,\n  getNextPageParam: (lastPage) =>\n    lastPage.hasMore ? lastPage.page + 1 : undefined,\n})\n```\n\nSee [Infinite Queries](./infinite-queries.md) for the controller-specific behavior.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: query-functions\ntitle: Query Functions\n---\n\nA query function can be any function that returns a promise. The promise should resolve data or throw an error.\n\n```ts\ncreateQueryController(this, {\n  queryKey: ['todos'],\n  queryFn: fetchTodos,\n})\n\ncreateQueryController(this, () => ({\n  queryKey: ['todo', this.todoId],\n  queryFn: () => fetchTodo(this.todoId),\n}))\n```\n\n## Handling Errors\n\nTanStack Query needs failed query functions to throw or return a rejected promise. Some clients do that automatically. The browser `fetch` API does not, so check `response.ok` yourself:\n\n```ts\nasync function fetchTodos(): Promise<Todo[]> {\n  const response = await fetch('/api/todos')\n\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    throw new Error('Failed to fetch todos')\n  }\n\n  return response.json() as Promise<Todo[]>\n}\n```\n\nThe thrown error is available on the query result:\n\n```ts\nconst query = this.todos()\n\nif (query.isError) {\n  return html`Error: ${query.error.message}`\n}\n```\n\n## Query Function Context\n\nTanStack Query passes a context object to every query function. It includes:\n\n- `queryKey`: the current query key\n- `client`: the `QueryClient`\n- `signal`: an `AbortSignal` for cancellation\n- `meta`: optional query metadata\n\n```ts\ncreateQueryController(this, {\n  queryKey: ['todos', { status: 'open' }],\n  queryFn: async ({ queryKey, signal }) => {\n    const [, filters] = queryKey\n    const response = await fetch(`/api/todos?status=${filters.status}`, {\n      signal,\n    })\n    if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Failed to fetch todos')\n    return response.json() as Promise<Todo[]>\n  },\n})\n```\n\nInfinite query functions also receive `pageParam`:\n\n```ts\ncreateInfiniteQueryController(this, {\n  queryKey: ['projects'],\n  queryFn: ({ pageParam }) => fetchProjectsPage(pageParam),\n  initialPageParam: 1,\n  getNextPageParam: (lastPage) =>\n    lastPage.hasMore ? lastPage.page + 1 : undefined,\n})\n```\n\nSee [Infinite Queries](./infinite-queries.md) for the controller-specific behavior.\n"}
